    [CI] Stage local actions in runner temp to reduce job setup time (#20068)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    #### Background
    
    Since runner-container-hooks v0.8.0 replaced shared volumes with
    exec-based file copying, the runner and job container workspaces may
    become inconsistent, causing local actions to fail with Can't find
    action.yml.
    
    This issue has been reported in [ascend-gha-runners/docs issues
    #146](https://github.com/ascend-gha-runners/docs/issues/146) and
    [actions/runner-container-hooks issues
    #337](https://github.com/actions/runner-container-hooks/issues/337). An
    upstream fix has been proposed in [actions/runner-container-hooks PR
    #445](https://github.com/actions/runner-container-hooks/pull/445), which
    restores a volume-backed implementation alongside the no-volume
    implementation, but it has not been merged yet.
    
    #### Previous workaround
    
    We previously used uses: `$/.github/actions/...` to work around the path
    resolution issue. However, this causes the runner to download the
    vllm-ascend repository during the Set up job phase, significantly
    increasing CI startup time. Additionally, this non-standard syntax
    requires extra actionlint ignore rules.
    <img width="2092" height="549" alt="image"
    src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c44389f8-d038-4173-ae87-13dc13055ec6"
    />
    
    #### Current approach
    
    This PR stages .github under `$RUNNER_TEMP/ci-workflow` and references
    local actions through uses:
    `./../../_temp/ci-workflow/.github/actions/....`
    
    This is intended to make action manifests resolvable through a standard
    relative uses: path while preserving reusable actions and removing the
    previous actionlint exceptions.
    
    The main trade-off is that this workaround depends on the runner's
    directory layout and introduces an additional copy step. If the
    workspace layout changes, the relative paths must be updated. It also
    requires the staged files to be visible to the runner.
    
    #### When can the official usage be restored
    Once the upstream issue is fixed and the fix is available in our runner
    environment, we can consider reverting to the standard uses:
    `./.github/actions/...` syntax.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
